      "text": "Note the identity\n\\[(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1) + (x^{2015} + x^{2014} + \\dots + x + 1) + \\dots + (x^{3} + x^{2} + x + 1) + (x + 1) = 2017x,\\]so we have\n\\[x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = 2017 x - x^{2017} + 2 = \\boxed{2}.\\]Plugging in the original equation into the identity gives\n\\[(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1) + 2 = x^{2017} + 2 = 2(x^{2017} - 2x) = 4(x - 1),\\]so $2 + 2 = 4(x - 1) \\Rightarrow x = 2.$  Therefore, $x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = 4(x - 1) = \\boxed{2}.$. The answer is 2",
