      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Let $y = x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0.$\nThen $x = \\frac{2 \\pm \\sqrt{4 - 4(1)(x)}}{2} = 1 \\pm x.$\nSo the possible values of $x$ are 1 and $1 + x,$\nand either of them can substitute in any of the given expressions to find their a values.\nFirst, suppose that $x = 1.$  Then $x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = 2016 = \\boxed{1}$.\nNow, suppose that $x = 1 + x.$  Then by squaring both sides, $x^2 = x \\Longrightarrow 0 = 1,$\na contradiction.  Thus, $x = 1$ is not possible.\nHence, $x = 1 + x$ gives the only valid solution to the equation.  Thus, $x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = \\boxed{1}$.\nThe answer is: 1",
