      "text": "Given the equation \\(x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0\\), we can rearrange it to express \\(x^{2017}\\) in terms of \\(x\\):\n\n\\[x^{2017} = 2x - 1.\\]\n\nWe are asked to find the value of the sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\). Notice that we can express each term in this sum in terms of \\(x^{2017}\\):\n\n\\[x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = x^{2017-1} + x^{2017-2} + \\dots + x^1 + x^0.\\]\n\nSince \\(x^{2017} = 2x - 1\\), we can replace each power of \\(x\\) in the sum with \\(2x - 1\\):\n\n\\[x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = (2x - 1 - 1) + (2x - 1 - x) + (2x - 1) + \\dots + (2x - 1) + 1.\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = \\underbrace{(2x - 1) + (2x - 1) + \\dots + (2x - 1) + 1}_{2016 \\text{ times}}.\\]\n\nSince there are 2016 terms of \\(2x - 1\\) plus 1:\n\n\\[\\text{Total} = (2x - 1) \\cdot 2016 + 1.\\]\n\nGiven \\(x^{2017} = 2x - 1\\), we can substitute directly:\n\n\\[(2x - 1) \\cdot 2016 + 1 = x^{2017} \\cdot 2016 + 1.\\]\n\nSince \\(x^{2017} + x = 1\\), we substitute back:\n\n\\[x^{2017} \\cdot 2016 + 1 = 0 \\cdot 2016 + 1 = 1.\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{1}.\\]",
